{title: There's Power in the Blood}
{artist: Lewis Ellis Jones}
{key: A}

{comment: Verse 1}
[A]Would you be free from your [D]burden of [A]sin?
There's [E]power in the blood, [A]power in the blood
Would you o'er evil the [D]victory [A]win?
There's [E]wonderful [E7]power in the [A]blood

{comment: Chorus}
There is [A]power, power, [D]wonder-working [A]power
In the blood of the [A]Lamb
There is power, power, wo[D]nder-working power
In the [E]precious [A/E]blood [E]of the [A]Lamb

{comment: Verse 2}
Would you be free from your passion and pride
There's power in the blood, power in the blood
Come for a cleansing to Calvary's tide
There's wonderful power in the blood

{comment: Verse 3}
Would you be whiter, much whiter than snow?
There's power in the blood, power in the blood
Sin stains are lost in it's life-giving flow
There's wonderful power in the blood

{comment: Verse 4}
Would you do service for Jesus your King?
There's power in the blood, power in the blood
Would you live daily His praises to sing?
There's wonderful power in the blood
